  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening humanitarian recovery and resilience for Communities in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 12 -month integrated response project will ensure holistic support across four counties in Kenya to communities facing ongoing food insecurity and the compounded impact of flooding. Interventions include targeted food security and livelihoods support; a holistic Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) approach; protection with focus on Gender Based Violence (GBV); and improved coordination between humanitarian actors connecting local and national levels to influence humanitarian policy. Specific flood response activities include distribution of Multi -Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCAs) and WASH Non -Food Items (NFIs) and targeting of the broader interventions to flood affected households and communities.</narrative>
  </description>
